\fs28 \cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 Cinema Challenge Hackathon dedicated to finding solutions for online cinema. The prize pool is $50 000. We invite data scientists, developers, managers, and designers to participate. Participation is possible both individually and as a team, depending on the chosen setting. What awaits the participants? \'95 $10 000 \'97 for first place in every challenge \'95 $5 000 \'97 for second place in every challenge \'95 500+ participants \'97 useful acquaintances \'95 professional and personal development You are allowed to use any external data source 10 submissions/day Deadline - 21.11.2020, 11.59 PM Your task is to predict the 5 most preferred **tv\\_show\\_id**s for each user from submission.csv, from the most preferred (#1) to the least preferred (#5). The preferences were calculated for the users using the subsequent 12 weeks (weeks 31-42) of historical views.\
